delim-one-type
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: `!Delim.shift[Int, Int, W](k => k(5))` asks for three type
  arguments and only one of them is news. R is already in the evidence
  `Prompted[R]`; F is the block's own row, which `Reader.ask` already
  takes from the `DirectCtx` (reader-env's RowOf). Make the evidence
  form `inline`, take F from the block and R from the evidence, so a
  direct block writes `!Delim.shift[Int](k => k(5))` — A alone, because
  A is the only thing the call site knows and inference cannot: a mark
  gives its argument no expected type.
files: src/main/scala/Delim.scala, src/test/scala/TestDelim.scala,
  docs/typepedia.md, CHANGELOG.md
